      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ce09c4ff1ef661188867ab5|full_name}: absolutely seconded. I have a pretty capable setup (7700K, 64GB RAM, 1080ti) and recording transparent footage nearly cripples my system at 1080p60, not to mention how ridiculously massive the recordings are. Alpha recording has been touted as a solution. Devs have historically refused to consider this because alpha recording is possible. \n\n\"Let them eat cake\"\n\nOne of the HUGE benefits of custom color backdrops is that you get to easily select a color with good contrast. If your avatar has green on it, the green screen kind of blows for lossy recording, which is what most of us would like to use.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
